***************************** T A L Y S **************************1325 1451  197
                                                                  1325 1451  198
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1325 1451  199
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1325 1451  200
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1325 1451  201
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1325 1451  202
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1325 1451  203
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1325 1451  204
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1325 1451  205
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1325 1451  206
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1325 1451  207
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1325 1451  208
stored in this data file:                                         1325 1451  209
                                                                  1325 1451  210
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1325 1451  211
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1325 1451  212
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1325 1451  213
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1325 1451  214
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1325 1451  215
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1325 1451  216
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1325 1451  217
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1325 1451  218
- Recoil data                                                     1325 1451  219
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1325 1451  220
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1325 1451  221
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1325 1451  222
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1325 1451  223
- Residual production cross sections                              1325 1451  224
                                                                  1325 1451  225
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1325 1451  226
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1325 1451  227
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1325 1451  228
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1325 1451  229
                                                                  1325 1451  230
